In this Archive you should find :atob     - OS968K binaryatob.c   - Sourcebtoa     - OS968K binarybtoa.c   - Sourcebtoa.1   - Unformatted manpagebtoa.man - Formatted manpagePlease look at the manpage for the basic info on btoa/atob. The onlydifference between the original version and the OSK version is that'atob' uses the directory defined in the environmental variable TMPDIR,for its temporary file. If TMPDIR is not set, it will just use the currentdirectory.Also, there appeared to be a bug??? in atob where the temp file was notdeleted. Either the original programmer(s) made an error and put ulink()in the wrong place in the code OR the unix unlink() works a bit differentthan the OSK unlink(). Under OSK, the file has to be closed for unlink towork, since one can't deincrement an open file. Perhaps this is notthe case in UNIX??? In any case it works now. ;)These programs were compiled on a Blackhawk MM/1 using Microware C V3.2under OSK V2.4. The source was obtained from the following Internet FTPsite:Host ftp.germany.eu.net    (192.76.144.75)Last updated 20:11  9 Feb 1995    Location: /pub/applications/archiver/compress/compress      FILE    -rw-r--r--    2483 bytes  20:00  7 Mar 1993  btoa.1      FILE    -rw-r--r--    2333 bytes  20:00  7 Mar 1993  btoa.c                                        Dean Leiber (Aditnavel@Delphi.com)                                        August 16, 1995